    "### 1. Lists — Lab Submissions Log\n",
    "Create a list `lab_submissions` with at least 8 entries (with some repeats — e.g. `\"OS\"` appearing 3 times, representing multiple lab submissions for that subject). Then:\n",
    "- Sort it alphabetically and print it.\n",
    "- Print how many times `\"OS\"` appears using `.count()`.\n",
    "- Print the last 3 submissions using slicing.\n",
    "- Overwrite the entry at index 0 with a different subject."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "12c58790",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# TODO: 1. Lists solution
lab_submissions = ["OS", "DBMS", "CN", "OS", "DAA", "DBMS", "OS", "SE"]

# Sort alphabetically
lab_submissions.sort()
print(f"Sorted submissions: {lab_submissions}")

# Count "OS"
print(f"Number of OS submissions: {lab_submissions.count('OS')}")

# Last 3 submissions
print(f"Last 3 submissions: {lab_submissions[-3:]}")

# Overwrite index 0
lab_submissions[0] = "AI"
print(f"Updated submissions: {lab_submissions}")\n"
   ]
